From ca11d3a8ea667f7ee07e8690b66fbf469dc3e7c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 20:51:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/28] WIP qsa3: packed-block WMMA prefill for the QSA sparse
 attention

Ports the Strix Halo branch's qsa-attn (rows/merge/attn kernels) onto the
delivery's GGML_OP_FLASH_ATTN_QSA:

- ggml.h/ggml.c: ggml_flash_attn_qsa_set_packed(src[7]=packed_keys,
  src[8]=packed_values); the pack itself is a pure graph composition
  (reshape+permute+cont), so no new ggml op.
- qwen4exp.cpp: build the packs for the prefill band (n_tps>=128, n_stream==1,
  F16/BF16 cache, n_kv%4==0) when GGML_CUDA_QSA3=1; a bf16 cache is cast to f16.
- fattn-qsa3.cu: rows+merge union descriptor (4 queries/group), and the
  16x16x16 F16 WMMA attn kernel (48 rows = 4 queries x 12 heads, 4 key blocks
  per chunk).  Supports both the mask and the derived-visibility (cell_vis/
  q_vis) paths.  Portable wrapper so gfx1201/gfx1100 still compile.
- gated prefill-only (q->ne[1]>=128 + RDNA3_5), so the W=1..8 band keeps the
  VEC kernel and width purity holds by construction.

gfx1151, IQ4_XS, bf16 KV: pp4096 833->875 (+5.0%), pp8192 787->860 (+9.3%);
wikitext PPL parity (c16384 3.3932/3.3900, c32768 4.3378/4.3353); greedy text
coherent, ~40 tokens identical then the approved prefill re-baseline.
